# Collapse content

A collapsible section built on the native `<details>`/`<summary>` elements. It renders as static HTML and toggles without JavaScript; a small script keeps `aria-expanded` in sync and supports deep-linking to a section by its `id`.

## Properties

| Property   | Type      | Default | Description                                                  |
|------------|-----------|---------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| `title`    | `string`  | —       | Required. The header text.                                   |
| `level`    | `string`  | `h3`    | Heading level for the title (`h1`–`h6`).                     |
| `expanded` | `boolean` | `false` | When true, the section starts open.                          |
| `id`       | `string`  | —       | Optional. Enables deep-linking to the section by URL hash.   |

